From 272194de1b452f710fb8eb3a75ec50e5306fbe27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:13:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(state): preserve missing-lease fencing and distinguish
 custody failures [daveey]

Reject the proposed INSERT-on-append recovery. Absence cannot distinguish an
unexpected loss from release, a successor that released, stale mutation or a
never-acquired writer. Keep the original fail-closed check and matching-row
expiry renewal. Report missing lease row versus holder mismatch explicitly;
user-facing copy no longer asserts a takeover from the generic error bucket.

Problem: session 20000101_000000_00000b failed after an Opus
response with session_persistence_failed:turn_lease.
Why 1: transcript guard rejected missing or mismatching custody.
Why 2: the generic copy incorrectly asserted takeover.
Root (happened): UNDETERMINED. A later missing row does not prove its state
at failure; no producer transition receipt establishes who removed it.
Root (not caught): diagnostics conflated missing custody with takeover;
original proposed tests replaced an intentional fail-closed contract.
Countermeasure: precise diagnostic reason without relaxing ownership.
Proof: independently reproduced 3 failed lifecycle regressions on 8887286
(release, successor-release, never acquired: all DID NOT RAISE). Revised
candidate: 68 tests passed across 4 targeted files including an independent
connection / Event-ordered successor-release late flush. Original Desktop
chat has later persisted successful final <message-id>; that is immediate recovery,
not evidence this patch was deployed or of vendor quota bucket sharing.
